## API types

Each release includes `[[ module_id ]]-api-types.tgz`, a private TypeScript package. A consuming module can install the matching release without publishing anything to npm:

```sh
yarn add --dev @[[ github_owner | lower ]]/[[ module_id ]]-api-types@https://github.com/[[ github_owner ]]/[[ repository_name ]]/releases/download/vX.Y.Z/[[ module_id ]]-api-types.tgz
```

Use `import type` from that package; it deliberately contains declarations only, not runtime code.
